    "title": "Tyler Water Utilities advances $19M wastewater project plan - NewsBreak",
    "text": "TYLER, Texas ( KETK )– Tyler Water Utilities announced on Wednesday that they will be moving forward with their wastewater system project. During a Tyler City Council meeting, the city approved two major wastewater projects as a part of the city’s agreement with the Environmental Protection Agency to improve their water infrastructure . The project will cost over $19 million and will provide a dependable wastewater system that will allow homes, businesses and schools to operate without disruption. “These projects are part of a long-term plan to invest in Tyler’s essential infrastructure,” Utilities Director Kate Dietz, P.E., said. “They will help protect our environment, improve system reliability, and ensure we meet the commitments we made to the EPA and our community.” As part of the project, the council approved a $16,179,339.80 contract with C&A Construction LCC to install 12,635 linear feet of new sanitary sewer lines ranging from 6 inches to 30 inches in diameter. The route will go from downtown and run through Midtown to the Charnwood District. Additionally, the council approved an engineering services contract with Pape Dawson Consulting Engineers LLC for $2,806,600 to design and oversee construction of improvements in Group 8. The upgrades are based on recent assessments of manholes across the city. Construction on the project is expected to be completed by March 2027 and is expected to help prevent sanitary sewer overflows. Additionally, the project will include new manholes, highway and railroad bores, creek crossings, laterals, pavement repairs and associated gravity sewer fixtures. You can now stream KETK and FOX51 News live 24/7 on your smart TV with KETK+ , our brand-new app! No antenna, cable, or satellite needed— watch for free, anytime. Just download it on your Roku, Apple TV, or Fire TV and start streaming. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KETK.com | FOX51.com.",
